# Requests to try with VS Code's REST Client extension.
# Start the server first (npm start), then click Send Request above any request.
# Every start of the server begins again from the same six pets.

### Every pet: 200
GET http://localhost:3100/pets

### Only the cats, Mochi and Juniper: 200
GET http://localhost:3100/pets?species=cat

### Mochi, the pet whose id is "2": 200
GET http://localhost:3100/pets/2

### No pet has the id 99: 404
GET http://localhost:3100/pets/99

### Add Waffles: 201, Waffles with the id "7" and the status "available"
POST http://localhost:3100/pets
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Waffles", "species": "dog", "age": 4, "traits": ["good with kids"] }

### A new pet with no name: 400
POST http://localhost:3100/pets
Content-Type: application/json

{ "species": "cat", "age": 2 }
